  "description": "If you've never been to a\nvelodrome or seen track racing on TV, this is what's called a \"track\niron.\" If you can call a bike made from aero-shape X-Fusion Alpha\ntubing an iron.\n\nSingle-gear and brakeless like the Track, this is a much more purposeful\nbike, made for racing on the steep banks of velodromes.\n\nYou can learn more about the Track Pro by reading the specs and looking\nat the photo than I can tell you in 200 words.\n\nI will say that the cutout in the back of the seat tube is NOT done by\nsawing out a section, flipping it and welding it back in. X-Fusion tubing\nis quite malleable before heat-treating; The cutout section is formed\nTHEN. Post heat-treating, X-Fusion will fiercely resist any such tweaking,\njust as it resists power-robbing deflection.\nCool, huh?",
